; The tagged-or-untagged set idiom (`x = #6.N([* a]) / [* a]`), non-generic flavor, pinned here on
; the EXPLICIT `@duplicates preserve` opt-out.
;
; A two-arm type choice whose arms are the SAME collection but for exactly one `Tagged(N)` encoding
; op is not two types: both arms denote the same logical value and which arm was written is an
; encoding detail (older on-chain data is untagged, the Conway-era Cardano ledger emits tag 258).
; cddl-codegen recognizes this structurally and collapses it into ONE transparent alias — never an
; enum — with the tag riding a `TagPresenceEncoding` var under --preserve-encodings so either wire
; arm roundtrips byte-exact, and defaulting to tagged otherwise. Near misses keep the two-variant
; enum (see tag_set_near_miss.cddl).
;
; These rules carry `; @duplicates preserve` DELIBERATELY: tag 258 is the IANA set tag, so a
; no-directive 258 idiom now DEFAULTS to `@duplicates reject` (the uniqueness twin — see
; tag_set_default.cddl). This fixture is the OPT-OUT contract: `preserve` restores the plain
; `Vec`/`NonEmptyVec` alias — the multi-era byte-exact reader for historical duplicate-bearing wire
; data — which is exactly the migration recipe the docs ship to consumers. The structural collapse
; itself is unchanged; only the effective duplicates policy is spelled explicitly. The trailing
; directive on a choice rule is RULE-level and must follow the LAST arm.
;
; - `int_set`   — the `[*]` (empty-allowed) flavor collapses to a transparent `Vec<u64>` alias.
; - `int_neset` — the `[+]` (non-empty) flavor collapses to a DISTINCT `NonEmptyVec<u64>` alias; the
;                 `[+]` invariant rides NonEmptyVec's single `TryFrom` door (the empty/non-empty
;                 split the CML hand impl wrongly conflated into one type).
; - `text_set`  — untagged arm FIRST: arm order is irrelevant to recognition.
; - `holder`    — embeds the collapsed rules in record-field position, including an OPTIONAL field, so
;                 the member-side (de)serialize and the optional-field wrapping both compile and
;                 round-trip.
int_set = #6.258([* uint]) / [* uint] ; @duplicates preserve
int_neset = #6.258([+ uint]) / [+ uint] ; @duplicates preserve
text_set = [* text] / #6.258([* text]) ; @duplicates preserve
holder = [s: int_set, ns: int_neset, ? t: text_set]
